abstract: >-
  The AB-cloud is a Hofstadter Hamiltonian decorated with topological vortices
  whose Aharonov-Bohm phases are derived from the non-trivial zeros of the
  Riemann zeta function. This repository is fully dedicated to the AB-cloud
  programme: five monograph editions (v22 RU/EN/ZH + original v21 RU/EN), the
  canonical 37-test two-pass Julia verification suite, an independent
  10-language verification stack with zeta-zero data up to 2M zeros, and a 3D
  lattice laboratory. Verified results: <r> = 0.5848 +/- 0.0260 vs GUE 0.5992;
  Montgomery test KS = 0.047 (p = 0.27, N = 500 certified zeros);
  Byers-Yang defect 3.5e-15; Connes self-duality (4 zero modes); Dirac
  dynamics R^2 = 0.9997.
